---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseSection from "../../components/CaseSection.astro";
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex";
import { caseStudyStyles } from "../../styles/caseStudyStyles";
import { portfolioStyles } from "../../styles/portfolioStyles";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Azure ML Lifecycle | Warre Snaet"
  description="MLOps coursework on Azure ML: training in the cloud, a model registry, an inference service, and CI/CD."
  kicker="Individual MLOps coursework, 2025"
  heading="Azure ML lifecycle"
  lead="A machine-learning workflow that can be rerun from start to finish. Data preparation and training run on Azure ML, and GitHub Actions downloads the registered model, serves it from a container, and checks it automatically."
  meta={[
    { label: "Role", value: "Individual implementation" },
    { label: "Stack", value: "Azure ML, TensorFlow, Python, FastAPI, Docker, GitHub Actions" },
    { label: "Model", value: "15-class sports-ball image classifier" },
  ]}
>
  <CaseSection label="Lifecycle" title="Everything around the model">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>In this course the model was only one piece of the system. Azure resources, data assets, environments, pipeline components, model versions, inference services, and deployment checks were all defined explicitly.</p>
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.architecture)} role="img" aria-label="Azure MLOps lifecycle from data assets to deployment verification">
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowRow)}>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Stage 1</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Azure data assets</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Fifteen classes resized to 64×64 in parallel jobs</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Stage 2</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Data split</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>80/20 train-test split within each class</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Stage 3</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Cloud training</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>A Keras CNN on an Azure ML compute cluster</span></div>
      </div>
      <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowArrow)}>↓ metrics + artifacts ↓</p>
      <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowRow)}>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Stage 4</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Model registry</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Versioned model with its metadata</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Serving</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>FastAPI inference</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Predictions, a health endpoint, and prediction history in PostgreSQL</span></div>
        <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNode)}><small {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.metadataLabel, caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>Delivery</small><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeContent)}>CI/CD workflow</strong><span {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.flowNodeDescription)}>Build, deploy, health check, and notification</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Implementation" title="What I built">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Automated the Azure setup: resource group, workspace, compute cluster, environments, components, and the data upload.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Built a four-stage Azure ML pipeline: fifteen independent preprocessing jobs, splitting, CNN training with augmentation and early stopping, and model registration.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Registered the trained model in Azure ML, so deployment starts from a registered model instead of a local file.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Built a FastAPI inference service and a Streamlit dashboard with Grad-CAM, backed by a history of predictions in PostgreSQL.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Containerized the system with Docker Compose. I also wrote Kubernetes manifests for it, but the workflow deploys with Docker Compose.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Used GitHub Actions to automate Azure setup, training, downloading the model, deployment on a self-hosted runner, health checks, a test prediction, deleting the Azure resources afterwards, and status messages to Discord.</li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Engineering" title="From raw data to a running service">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list, caseStudyStyles.factsList)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Versioning</strong>Data assets, environments, and models have versions in Azure ML, and every workflow run tags its container images with the run number.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Cloud execution</strong>Preprocessing and training run on the Azure ML resources I created, not only on a local machine.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Deployment checks</strong>The workflow checks the service's health, runs a test prediction, and posts the pipeline status to Discord.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Explainability</strong>The Streamlit dashboard uses Grad-CAM to show which parts of an image influenced a prediction.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Kubernetes manifests</strong>The manifests include probes, resource limits, persistent storage, secrets, and two API replicas. I didn't deploy them to a cluster.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Scope</strong>Training and model registration ran in the cloud on Azure ML. Serving ran with Docker Compose on a self-hosted machine, not on a live production cluster.</li>
    </ul>
    <div {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.links)}><a {...stylex.attrs(portfolioStyles.link, caseStudyStyles.importantLink)} href="https://github.com/SnaetWarre/mlops-sports-ball-classification">View repository ↗</a></div>
  </CaseSection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
